@startuml 12-sequence-status-change-notify
title Sequence 2 - Order status change -> observers (UI, notification, analytics)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

participant "OrderLifecycleService\n(Restaurant app stand-in)" as Lifecycle
participant "OrderRepository" as Repo
participant "Order" as Order
participant "OrderState\n(CreatedState)" as State
participant "SynchronousOrderEventPublisher" as Publisher
participant "OrderTrackingViewModel\n(listener)" as VM
participant "View" as View
participant "NotificationOrderListener" as NL
participant "MultiChannelNotifier" as Notifier
participant "Notification\n(OrderUpdateNotification)" as Notification
participant "NotificationChannel\n(Push / SMS / Email)" as Channel
participant "OrderStatusCounter" as Counter

Lifecycle -> Repo : findById(id)
Repo --> Lifecycle : Order
Lifecycle -> Order : confirm()

group inside Order.operate(), holding the order lock
  Order -> State : confirm(context)
  alt operation allowed in this state
    State -> Order : context.transitionTo(ConfirmedState)
    note right of Order
      records StatusTransition,
      calls next.onEnter(context),
      adds OrderStatusChanged to `pending`
    end note
  else operation not allowed in this state
    State --> Order : throws IllegalOrderOperationException
    Order --> Lifecycle : exception (no state change, no event)
  end
end
note over Order : lock released BEFORE publishing

Order -> Publisher : publish(OrderStatusChanged)

Publisher -> VM : onOrderStatusChanged(event)
VM -> VM : uiState.value = OrderTrackingUiState.from(event)
VM --> View : StateFlow emits (collected on the main thread)

Publisher -> NL : onOrderStatusChanged(event)
NL -> Notifier : notifyOrderUpdate(customer, orderId, status.customerMessage)
note right of NL : notifyUrgent(...) instead when event.current.urgent\n(only CANCELLED); the listener never compares statuses
loop each channel the customer opted into
  Notifier -> Notification : <<create>> OrderUpdateNotification(channel, orderId, text)
  Notifier -> Notification : send(customer)
  Notification -> Channel : deliver(recipient, buildMessage())
end

Publisher -> Counter : onOrderStatusChanged(event)
Counter -> Counter : count(CONFIRMED)++

Order --> Lifecycle : done
Lifecycle -> Repo : save(order)
note over Publisher
  A failing listener is isolated (the others still run).
  OrderTrackingViewModel cancels its Subscription in onCleared().
end note
@enduml
